# File:       Opus/.gitignore
# Component:  Opus
# Author:     Jacob Chacko
#
# What never gets committed: build output, runtime data, and the caches
# each tool leaves behind.

# Compiled output
Conductor/build/
Ensemble/build/

# Content/ is committed: the configs and the default schemas live there.
# The configs hold a placeholder database password, and Postgres only
# listens on this machine, so that's fine.  The logs stay out, since they
# change every run.  Content/Assets/ is the purchased art, which stays out
# for now.  Content/world/ is the game's save, the chunks players have
# changed, which changes every time somebody digs.
Content/Assets/
Content/logs/
Content/world/
# Ensemble's Assets/ is mostly the purchased art and what Unity makes from
# it, so it stays out, all but the four folders that are ours: Editor/ for
# the editor plugins, Code/ for the plain C# (the networking, say),
# Scripts/ for the scripts and Data/ for our own data files (the HUD's
# layouts, say).  Unity keeps a .meta beside every folder, so each folder's
# .meta comes in with it.  Purchased art never goes in those four.
Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/Assets/*
!Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/Assets/Editor/
!Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/Assets/Editor.meta
!Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/Assets/Code/
!Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/Assets/Code.meta
!Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/Assets/Scripts/
!Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/Assets/Scripts.meta
!Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/Assets/Data/
!Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/Assets/Data.meta
Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/Packages/
Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/UserSettings/
# UI Builder writes the UXML schemas beside Assets/ and rewrites them
# itself, so they're Unity's, not ours.
Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/UIElementsSchema/
# The C# project and solution files.  Unity makes them, and rewrites them on
# every compile, so a commit of them was only ever Unity's last rewrite and
# stopped a checkout of another branch (2026-10-02).
Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/*.csproj
Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/*.sln
Ensemble/dev/Opus.Ensemble/*.slnx
# A change saved from the web admin, waiting for its reboot.  It's this
# machine's, not the repo's.
Content/cfg/*.wait4server
# The TLS private key.  The certificate beside it is committed (clients
# need a copy); the key never leaves the machine it was made on.  Not
# from anywhere in Opus: a copy of it went in under Ensemble once
# (2026-10-02), so no .key file is ever committed.
*.key
*.key.meta

# Rust, in case target/ ever lands in dev/
**/target/

# Python's compiled cache, from running the test client
**/__pycache__/

# Unity caches
Ensemble/dev/**/[Ll]ibrary/
Ensemble/dev/**/[Tt]emp/
Ensemble/dev/**/[Oo]bj/
Ensemble/dev/**/[Ll]ogs/
Ensemble/dev/**/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/

# Godot cache
**/.godot/

# IDE and OS clutter
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Soundcheck's build output: what dotnet makes beside the project, and
# the packages folder like the other two components'.
Soundcheck/build/
Soundcheck/dev/bin/
Soundcheck/dev/obj/
# The stamp of the shipped client (patch_manifest.json), and the client
# itself if it sits there.  This machine's, not the repo's.
Content/patch/
